    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying a prime position within the highly regarded Silchester Park, No. 100 is a\nbright and spacious semi-detached home extending to approximately 123 sq.m.\n(1,324 sq.ft.). Well presented throughout, the property offers generously proportioned\naccommodation ideally suited to modern living, together with significant scope to\nextend and further enhance, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nA welcoming entrance hall leads to a bright living room overlooking the front garden,\nwith double doors opening into a family room where French doors provide direct\naccess to the generous rear garden. The kitchen/dining room is positioned off the\nfamily room, creating an excellent flow for everyday living. The original garage has\nbeen thoughtfully converted to provide a highly versatile room, ideal as a home\noffice, study or playroom and is complemented by a separate utility room.\n\nUpstairs, there are three well-appointed bedrooms, a family bathroom and separate\nWC. Outside, the large rear garden provides excellent space for children to play,\noutdoor dining and future extension potential. The property further benefits from a\nside entrance and an attic suitable for conversion, subject to planning permission.\nCombining flexible accommodation with excellent future potential, this is a home that\ncan readily adapt to changing needs over time.\n\nSilchester Park is widely regarded as one of Glenageary's most sought-after\nresidential developments. Located close to the seafront and within easy reach of\nSandycove, Glasthule, Dalkey and Dún Laoghaire, the property enjoys a wealth of\namenities on its doorstep. A particular feature is the exclusive private resident's park\nto the rear, providing a secure and spacious green area for children to enjoy. The\narea is also well served by highly regarded primary and secondary schools, excellent\npublic transport links including the DART, local shops, cafés, restaurants, sporting\nclubs and a wide range of recreational facilities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Special Features</li><li> Approx. 123 sq.m. (1,324 sq.ft.) of accommodation</li><li> Bright and spacious semi-detached home</li><li> Large rear garden</li><li> Private residents park</li><li> Living room with double doors opening to family room</li><li> Family room with French doors to rear garden</li><li> Kitchen/dining room</li><li> Flexible converted garage suitable as a home office, study or playroom</li><li> Separate utility room</li><li> Three bedrooms</li><li> Family bathroom and separate WC</li><li> Side entrance</li><li> Significant potential to extend, subject to planning permission</li><li> Attic suitable for future conversion, subject to planning permission</li><li> Double-glazed windows</li><li> Driveway providing off-street parking</li><li> Quiet and mature residential setting</li><li> Walking distance to the seafront, Sandycove, Glasthule, Dalkey and Dún Laoghaire</li><li> Excellent choice of schools, transport links, shops and leisure amenities nearby</ul>"
      },
